      "extract": "For a knot $K \\subset S^3$, let $n(K)$ denote a tubular neighborhood of $K$ and let $M_K:=\\overline{ S^3\\setminus n(K)}$ denote the exterior of $K$. Let $\\langle \\mu, \\lambda \\rangle$ be the canonical meridian--longitude basis of $H_1 (\\bdy n(K))$. An element $a/b \\in {\\QQ}\\cup \\{ 1/0\\}$ is called a \\emph{boundary slope} of $K$ if there is a properly embedded essential surface $(S, \\bdy S) \\subset (M_K, \\bdy n(K))$,",
      "extractCut": true
    },
