          "heading": false
        }
      ],
      "extract": "The family of 2-fusion knots is a two-parameter family of closed 3-braids denoted by $$\\{ K(m_1, m_2) \\mid m_1, m_2\\in \\ZZ\\}.$$ For the precise definition and description see \\cite {GV, DG}. Note that $K(m_1, m_2)$ is a torus knot if $m_2 \\in \\{-1,0\\}$. In fact, $K(m_1, 0) = T(2, 2m_1 + 1)$ and $K(m_1, -1) = T(2, 2m_1 -3)$. It is known that $K(m_1, m_2)$ is hyperbolic if $m_1 \\notin \\{0, 1\\}$, $m_2 \\notin \\{-1,0\\}$",
      "extractCut": true
    },
